{
  "choices": [
    {
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "index": 0,
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"status\": \"updated\",\n  \"chapter_updates\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch3\",\n      \"updated_plan\": {\n        \"chapter_id\": \"Ch3\",\n        \"units\": [\n          {\n            \"unit_id\": \"U3_2\",\n            \"substantive_point\": \"肌苷通过直接抑制肿瘤细胞泛素激活酶 UBA6 解除其对 FAT10 硫酯键形成及炎症信号通路的抑制，增强 MHC-I 表达与 T 细胞杀伤敏感性；CheckMate 025 队列确立了基线血浆肌苷与抗 PD-1 总生存期的正向关联，但该关联仅基于循环水平，人体 TME 内肌苷的实测浓度尚未获得，血浆数据只能作为系统性暴露的间接代理。\",\n            \"cases\": [\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"4T1 与 B16-GMCSF 小鼠肿瘤细胞系；LiP-SMap 化学蛋白质组学筛选；CRISPR 介导的 Uba6 敲除与回补实验；体外 T 细胞 - 肿瘤细胞共培养杀伤测定。\",\n                \"finding\": \"肌苷直接结合并抑制 UBA6 活性，减少其与 E2 连接酶 USE1 的相互作用及 FAT10 硫酯键形成；UBA6 抑制导致肿瘤细胞 TNF-α/IFN 响应基因上调，MHC-I 表面表达增加，对 T 细胞介导的杀伤更敏感。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0582\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"CheckMate 025 临床试验队列（n=394 接受 nivolumab，n=349 接受 everolimus）；基线血浆非靶向代谢组学；按代谢物中位数分层 Kaplan-Meier 生存分析。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在 CheckMate 025 肾细胞癌（RCC）队列中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的基线血浆肌苷高水平者中位总生存期为 33 个月，显著高于低水平组的 22 个月；该关联在依维莫司对照组中不存在。研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未能在其 22 人的多癌种人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度，仅以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性代理。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0582\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"体外人源 PBMC 培养与小鼠异种移植模型；流式细胞术检测细胞因子分泌；同位素示踪代谢通量分析。\",\n                \"finding\": \"肌苷由假长双歧杆菌等产生，通过结合 T 细胞腺苷 A2A 受体（A2AR）激活 cAMP-CREB 通路促进 Th1 分化，并在葡萄糖受限 TME 中作为替代碳源维持效应 T 细胞存活。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"364d5abc343a02132e4f3f24c0b441cb277190f2\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0124\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"工程化大肠杆菌表面展示 ADA 模型；B16-F10 黑色素瘤与 WEHI-3 AML 小鼠模型；LC-MS 评估代谢动力学与细胞毒性恢复。\",\n                \"finding\": \"腺苷脱氨酶（ADA）将免疫抑制性的腺苷转化为肌苷，体外证实腺苷暴露抑制 NK/T 细胞杀伤力而转化为肌苷可恢复功能；肌苷在血浆中半衰期约 15 小时，远长于腺苷的极短半衰期。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0584\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"ordered_development\": \"阐述肌苷进入肿瘤细胞的转运与 UBA6 结合的生化验证 -> 描述 UBA6 缺失/抑制后 MHC-I 上调与抗原呈递增强的细胞表型 -> 汇报 CheckMate 025 血浆肌苷与 OS 关联的临床数据并标注血浆代理局限 -> 区分肌苷的肿瘤内在作用与 T 细胞外在作用 -> 阐述腺苷→肌苷转化动力学与 ENT 转运体依赖对机制解读的约束。\",\n            \"paragraph_briefs\": [\n              {\n                \"paragraph_id\": \"U3_2_P01\",\n                \"unit_id\": \"U3_2\",\n                \"point\": \"详述肌苷靶向 UBA6 的生化结合验证、遗传学回补实验及对肿瘤细胞抗原呈递通路的分子重塑。\",\n                \"development\": \"整合 P0582 的 LiP-SMap 筛选（4T1 裂解物中鉴定出 23 个肌苷结合候选蛋白，仅 UBA6 缺失显著增强 T 细胞杀伤）、体外硫酯酶活性测定（肌苷减少 UBA6-USE1 互作并降低 FAT10 硫酯键形成）及 CRISPR 敲除数据（UBA6 缺失消除肌苷增敏效应），构建\"肌苷-UBA6-USE1-FAT10\"信号轴。补充 UFD 结构域删除实验证实肌苷结合位点。\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\"P0582\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"paragraph_id\": \"U3_2_P02\",\n                \"unit_id\": \"U3_2\",\n                \"point\": \"汇报 CheckMate 025 队列中血浆肌苷水平与抗 PD-1 治疗总生存期的定量关联，并明确标注血浆数据作为系统性暴露代理的局限。\",\n                \"development\": \"基于 P0582 的临床队列数据，报告 nivolumab 组高/低肌苷中位 OS（33 vs 22 个月）及 everolimus 对照组无此关联的治疗特异性。同时指出：该研究在 22 人多癌种队列中因样本完整性问题未能直接检测肌苷浓度，仅以 UBA6 IHC 作为通路活性代理；血浆肌苷水平受饮食、肠道菌群周转及肾脏清除率影响，不能等同于 TME 局部有效浓度。此处仅标注代理局限，跨代谢物的 TME 浓度缺口总论由 U3_5 承担。\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\"P0582\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"paragraph_id\": \"U3_2_P03\",\n                \"unit_id\": \"U3_2\",\n                \"point\": \"区分肌苷的肿瘤内在作用（UBA6 抑制）与 T 细胞外在作用（A2AR 激活/碳源补充），避免机制混淆。\",\n                \"development\": \"结合 P0124 与 P0584，对比肌苷在肿瘤细胞内直接抑制 UBA6（P0582）与在 T 细胞内通过 A2AR/cAMP 通路促进 Th1 分化（P0124）或作为替代碳源维持效应 T 细胞存活（P0124）的平行机制。引用 P0251 关于双歧杆菌通过肌苷-A2AR 轴增强 T 细胞活性的还原论路径，并指出 P0584 中 ADA 工程菌将腺苷转化为肌苷以恢复 NK/T 细胞功能的临床前证据。\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\"P0124\", \"P0251\", \"P0584\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"paragraph_id\": \"U3_2_P04\",\n                \"unit_id\": \"U3_2\",\n                \"point\": \"阐述腺苷→肌苷转化动力学、ENT 转运体依赖及肌苷多源性对机制解读的约束，为 U3_5 的跨代谢物浓度缺口评估提供肌苷案例的药代动力学背景。\",\n                \"development\": \"综合 P0582 讨论部分与 P0584 综述：腺苷在体内半衰期极短（约 10 秒）且血浆清除快（约 30 秒），而肌苷半衰期较长（约 15 小时），这一动力学差异决定了 TME 内肌苷的维持依赖于持续的腺苷转化与 ENT 转运体摄取。肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞自身分泌），且 P0582 指出其效应依赖肿瘤细胞基础 UBA6 表达水平（低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。这些药代动力学与来源复杂性约束了从体外 100 μM 人工浓度向人体 TME 有效浓度的外推，但本段不展开跨代谢物 TME 浓度缺口的系统评估（由 U3_5 承担）。\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\"P0582\", \"P0584\"]\n              }\n            ],\n            \"supporting_studies\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"核心文献，证实肌苷直接结合 UBA6 解除 MHC-I 抑制，并指出人体肿瘤内实测浓度缺失的关键转化缺口。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0582\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"阐释双歧杆菌来源肌苷经 A2AR/cAMP 通路促进 Th1 分化及作为替代碳源维持效应 T 细胞存活的平行机制。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"364d5abc343a02132e4f3f24c0b441cb277190f2\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0124\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供腺苷脱氨酶将免疫抑制性腺苷转化为肌苷的药代动力学数据，说明肌苷半衰期延长对微环境暴露的意义。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0584\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"对比生态与还原论方法，明确双歧杆菌通过肌苷-A2AR 轴增强 T 细胞活性的分子路径，支撑机制解析。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"68b67449fc944c707f68e31b629b3909e59b29ea\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0251\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供肌苷联合 ICI 治疗晚期实体瘤的首个随机对照临床 II 期数据（PFS HR=0.63），为外源性肌苷补充的临床可行性提供初步证据，但该研究未测量内源性 TME 肌苷浓度。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:272644866\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0588\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"建立基于单细胞分辨率的药物诱导 TME 重塑量化框架，发现别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性和 T 细胞功能；人类证据仅为回顾性队列中痛风药使用与生存期的关联，非直接肌苷浓度测量。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286644045\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0593\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"synthesis\": \"肌苷的作用具有明确的靶点特异性：它通过直接抑制肿瘤细胞 UBA6 解除对 MHC-I 与炎症通路的转录后抑制（P0582），同时作为 T 细胞的代谢燃料与 A2AR 配体协同增效（P0124, P0584）。CheckMate 025 队列提供了循环肌苷预测 OS 的临床关联（P0582），但该关联仅基于血浆水平；在 22 人多癌种队列中，作者因样本完整性问题未能直接测量肌苷，仅以 UBA6 表达作为间接代理。P0588 的 II 期试验证实外源性肌苷补充可延长 PFS（HR=0.63），但同样未提供内源性 TME 浓度数据。腺苷→肌苷的快速转化动力学（腺苷半衰期约 10 秒，肌苷约 15 小时）、ENT 转运体依赖及肌苷的多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞）进一步约束了从体外 100 μM 人工浓度向人体 TME 有效浓度的外推。跨代谢物的 TME 绝对浓度缺口及其对因果推断的系统性限制，将在 U3_5 中统一评估。\",\n            \"transition\": \"肌苷案例揭示了代谢物机制确证对局部浓度数据的依赖。然而，这一困境并非肌苷独有——SCFAs、胆汁酸、色氨酸代谢物同样面临血浆/粪便代理与 TME 实测之间的鸿沟。下一单元将从跨代谢物视角系统评估这一转化缺口。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"unit_id\": \"U3_5\",\n            \"substantive_point\": \"现有证据高度依赖血浆或粪便代谢物浓度作为系统性暴露代理，人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内代谢物的绝对生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的直接定量关联构成跨代谢物类别的关键转化缺口；体外人工设定浓度、药代动力学限制、组织递送障碍及因果推断边界共同约束了从动物模型向人体临床的翻译。\",\n            \"cases\": [\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者小型队列；肿瘤组织免疫组化（IHC）检测 UBA6；基线血浆代谢组学。\",\n                \"finding\": \"作者明确指出由于临床样本完整性问题，未能在其 22 人的多癌种人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度，仅能以 UBA6 蛋白表达作为通路活性的间接代理指标。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0582\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"跨多项已发表研究的综合评述；临床队列与临床前模型的对照分析。\",\n                \"finding\": \"多数机制证据来自小鼠模型，人体内的确切浓度 - 效应关系尚不明确；血浆/粪便浓度不能完全代表 TME 暴露水平，需警惕将动物模型浓度直接外推至人体的风险。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0363\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"体外细胞系培养实验；药代动力学参数推导。\",\n                \"finding\": \"虽然体外实验使用 100 μM 肌苷处理肿瘤细胞以观察 UBA6 抑制，但这属于人工设定浓度而非人体内源性实测值；体内微环境浓度受局部血流灌注、细胞摄取速率及降解酶活性多重制约。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0584\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"药理学与肿瘤生理学理论推导；已有药物递送障碍文献综述。\",\n                \"finding\": \"代谢物在 TME 中的实际递送效率受限于血管通透性、间质液压及细胞膜转运体（如 ENT）的表达丰度，导致全身循环浓度与局部有效浓度之间存在显著脱节。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"b4de79d677aec2f2b495ddebba1aaf8a77cffc38\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0413\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"ordered_development\": \"评估血浆/粪便代谢组学作为系统性暴露代理的跨代谢物效能与固有偏差 -> 剖析 TME 绝对浓度缺失对机制确证与剂量优化的跨代谢物阻碍 -> 提出填补浓度缺口的未来技术路线与研究范式。\",\n            \"paragraph_briefs\": [\n              {\n                \"paragraph_id\": \"U3_5_P01\",\n                \"unit_id\": \"U3_5\",\n                \"point\": \"客观评估当前血浆/粪便代谢组学作为 ICI 疗效预测工具的跨代谢物效能与固有偏差。\",\n                \"development\": \"基于 P0582 与 P0363，承认宏观代谢物检测在临床可行性上的优势（如 CheckMate 025 血浆肌苷与 OS 的关联），同时指出其跨代谢物的共性局限：无法区分游离态与结合态、无法反映组织滞留时间、受饮食/抗生素/肾脏清除率强烈干扰。P0363 进一步强调多数机制证据来自小鼠模型，人体内的确切浓度-效应关系尚不明确，血浆/粪便浓度不能完全代表 TME 暴露水平。此评估覆盖 SCFAs、肌苷、胆汁酸、色氨酸代谢物等所有本章讨论的代谢物类别，而非仅限于肌苷。\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\"P0582\", \"P0363\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"paragraph_id\": \"U3_5_P02\",\n                \"unit_id\": \"U3_5\",\n                \"point\": \"深入剖析人体 TME 内代谢物绝对浓度数据缺失对机制研究与临床转化的跨代谢物阻碍，统一标注体外人工浓度、药代动力学限制与组织递送障碍。\",\n                \"development\": \"结合 P0584 与 P0413 的药代动力学与递送障碍分析，构建跨代谢物的浓度缺口框架：（1）体外人工浓度（如 100 μM 肌苷）非内源性实测值，不能直接外推为人体 TME 有效浓度；（2）代谢物在 TME 中的实际递送效率受血管通透性、间质液压及细胞膜转运体（如 ENT）表达丰度制约，导致全身循环浓度与局部有效浓度脱节（P0413）；（3）P0363 警示跨物种外推风险，动物模型中的高浓度干预策略难以直接翻译至临床。肌苷作为本章最详细的案例（U3_2 已阐述其 UBA6 机制），在此仅作为例证说明 TME 浓度缺失如何阻碍确定有效抑制 UBA6 所需的浓度阈值，不重复展开其分子机制细节。\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\"P0584\", \"P0413\", \"P0363\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"paragraph_id\": \"U3_5_P03\",\n                \"unit_id\": \"U3_5\",\n                \"point\": \"规划填补 TME 浓度缺口的未来技术路线与研究范式。\",\n                \"development\": \"提出引入原位微透析（microdialysis）、基质辅助激光解吸电离质谱成像（MALDI-MSI）及配对组织-血液纵向采样，以建立\"局部浓度-受体占有率-临床结局\"的直接定量映射。强调未来研究需跨越单一代谢物视角，在 SCFAs、胆汁酸、色氨酸代谢物等多个类别中同步建立 TME 浓度基线，并将浓度数据与 ICI 临床结局（ORR、PFS、OS）进行配对统计分析，从而将当前的系统性关联证据推进为局部因果确证。\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\"P0582\", \"P0363\", \"P0413\"]\n              }\n            ],\n            \"supporting_studies\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"明确指出因样本完整性问题未能在人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度，仅能以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性代理，为 TME 浓度缺口提供具体例证。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0582\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"强调多数机制证据来自小鼠模型，血浆/粪便浓度不能完全代表 TME 暴露水平，警示跨物种外推风险，为跨代谢物浓度缺口评估提供框架性判断。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0363\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"指出体外有效浓度（如 100 μM 肌苷）属人工设定而非内源性实测值，体内浓度受血流灌注与降解酶多重制约，为体外-体内浓度脱节提供具体例证。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0584\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"从药理学角度分析代谢物在 TME 中的递送效率受血管通透性、间质液压及转运体限制，导致全身循环与局部有效浓度脱节，为跨代谢物递送障碍提供机制框架。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"b4de79d677aec2f2b495ddebba1aaf8a77cffc38\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0413\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"synthesis\": \"本章所有代谢物类别（SCFAs、肌苷、胆汁酸、色氨酸衍生物）的机制假设均建立在\"系统性暴露代理\"之上。P0582 的坦诚声明代表了当前领域的普遍困境：已知高血浆肌苷预示更长 OS，但不知肿瘤实质内究竟需要多少 μM 的肌苷才能饱和抑制 UBA6。P0363 与 P0413 进一步指出，血浆/粪便浓度受饮食、肾脏清除率及肠道菌群周转率的强烈干扰，无法精确反映 TME 局部的真实化学梯度；代谢物在 TME 中的实际递送效率受血管通透性、间质液压及转运体表达丰度制约。这一跨代谢物的浓度缺口不仅阻碍了代谢物补充剂的精准给药，也使得许多基于动物模型的高浓度干预策略难以直接翻译至临床。当前证据仅能确立关联，不能确证因果。\",\n            \"transition\": \"综上所述，微生物代谢物通过精密的分子网络深刻重塑了实体瘤的免疫景观，但跨越从系统性关联到局部因果确证的鸿沟，仍需下一代空间与动态监测技术的介入。\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unit_id_remap\": {\n    \"U3_2\": [\"U3_2\"],\n    \"U3_5\": [\"U3_5\"]\n  }\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "Let me analyze the task carefully.\n\nThe selection context identifies that U3_2 and U3_5 both use P0582, P0584, and P0413 to argue about inosine TME concentration gaps, creating repetition risk. The improvement focus is:\n1. U3_2 should retain inosine-UBA6-USE1-FAT10 mechanism, CheckMate 025 plasma inosine-OS association, and plasma exposure proxy limitations\n2. U3_5 should take on cross-metabolite TME absolute concentration gap assessment, avoiding repeating inosine molecular mechanism details\n3. Uniformly annotate in vitro artificial concentrations, pharmacokinetic limitations, tissue delivery barriers, and causal inference boundaries\n\nLet me examine the current U3_2 and U3_5 plans:\n\n**U3_2 (current):**\n- substantive_point: Inosine directly targets tumor cell UBA6, releasing inhibition of inflammatory signaling and MHC-I expression, enhancing tumor-intrinsic immunogenicity and T cell killing sensitivity; however, human TME inosine absolute physiological concentration data is missing, existing clinical associations are only based on plasma levels.\n- Cases include P0582 (mechanism + CheckMate 025 + TME gap), P0124 (A2AR/cAMP), P0584 (ADA engineering)\n- Paragraph briefs:\n  - P01: UBA6 mechanism (P0582)\n  - P02: CheckMate 025 plasma data + TME gap (P0582)\n  - P03: Distinguish tumor-intrinsic vs T cell extrinsic mechanisms (P0124, P0251, P0584)\n  - P04: TME concentration gap + PK challenges (P0582, P0584)\n\n**U3_5 (current):**\n- substantive_point: Existing evidence highly relies on plasma/fecal metabolite concentrations as systemic exposure proxies; human TME absolute physiological concentrations and direct quantitative associations with ICI efficacy constitute key translational gaps, especially inosine TME measurement data absence.\n- Cases include P0582 (TME gap), P0363 (cross-species extrapolation), P0584 (in vitro artificial concentrations), P0413 (delivery barriers)\n- Paragraph briefs:\n  - P01: Evaluate plasma/fecal metabolomics efficacy and biases (P0582, P0363)\n  - P02: Analyze TME concentration gap barriers, especially inosine case (P0584, P0413)\n  - P03: Future technical routes (P0582, P0363, P0413)\n\nThe problem is clear: U3_2_P04 and U3_5_P02 both discuss the TME concentration gap for inosine, creating redundancy. The improvement focus suggests:\n- U3_2 should focus on the mechanism and clinical association, mentioning the plasma proxy limitation briefly but not deeply elaborating the TME gap\n- U3_5 should be the cross-metabolite assessment of TME concentration gaps, using inosine as one example but not re-explaining its molecular mechanism\n\nLet me now plan the edits:\n\n**U3_2 edits:**\n- Keep P01 (UBA6 mechanism) as is\n- Keep P02 (CheckMate 025) but tighten the TME gap mention to just noting it as a limitation of plasma proxy, not elaborating\n- Keep P03 (distinguish mechanisms) as is\n- Modify P04: Instead of deeply elaborating TME concentration gap (which U3_5 will do), this paragraph should focus on the pharmacokinetic context (adenosine→inosine conversion, half-life differences) as it relates to understanding the mechanism's physiological relevance, and briefly note that TME quantification remains unresolved, deferring to U3_5 for the broader assessment. Actually, looking more carefully, P04 currently says \"明确标注人体 TME 内肌苷绝对浓度数据的缺失现状及药代动力学挑战\" - this overlaps heavily with U3_5. \n\nThe better approach: U3_2_P04 should focus on the PK context that is specific to the inosine mechanism (adenosine half-life ~10s, inosine ~15h, ENT transporter dependency) as it constrains mechanism interpretation, but NOT do the full TME gap assessment. The full gap assessment belongs in U3_5.\n\nActually, re-reading the improvement focus more carefully: \"U3_2 保留肌苷-UBA6-USE1-FAT10 机制、CheckMate 025 血浆肌苷与 OS 关联，以及血浆暴露代理的局限\" - so U3_2 should mention plasma proxy limitations but the deep TME gap analysis goes to U3_5.\n\nLet me restructure:\n\n**U3_2 revised:**\n- P01: UBA6 mechanism (unchanged)\n- P02: CheckMate 025 + note that this is plasma data serving as systemic exposure proxy, with the specific limitation that no TME measurement was possible (brief mention, not elaboration)\n- P03: Distinguish tumor-intrinsic vs T cell mechanisms (unchanged)\n- P04: Reframe to focus on PK constraints specific to interpreting the mechanism (adenosine→inosine conversion kinetics, ENT transporter requirement, multi-source origin of inosine) rather than the broad TME gap assessment. The paragraph should note that these PK features constrain mechanism validation but defer the systematic assessment of concentration gaps to U3_5.\n\n**U3_5 revised:**\n- P01: Broaden to assess plasma/fecal metabolomics as systemic exposure proxies across ALL metabolite classes (not just inosine), using P0363's framework. Inosine is one example but not the focus.\n- P02: The TME concentration gap as a cross-metabolite problem. Use P0584 (in vitro artificial concentrations), P0413 (delivery barriers), and P0363 (cross-species extrapolation). Inosine serves as the most developed case study but the paragraph should frame this as a general problem affecting SCFAs, bile acids, tryptophan metabolites too. Avoid re-explaining UBA6 mechanism.\n- P03: Future technical routes (unchanged in spirit but ensure it's framed as cross-metabolite, not inosine-specific)\n\nLet me also check: the supporting studies and cases need to be adjusted accordingly.\n\nFor U3_2, I should remove P0584 from the TME gap paragraph (P04) since that's more U3_5's territory. P0584 can stay in P03 for the ADA/adenosine→inosine conversion mechanism.\n\nFor U3_5, I should ensure P0582 is used for the general statement about TME measurement failure (not for re-explaining UBA6 mechanism), and P0584/P0413 for the broader PK/delivery constraints.\n\nLet me also check if P0588 (the Phase 2 inosine trial) should be incorporated. Looking at the current U3_2 supporting_studies, P0588 is listed. The Phase 2 trial data (inosine supplementation + ICI, PFS improvement) is relevant to U3_2 as it shows clinical translation of the inosine mechanism. But it should be noted as exogenous supplementation, not endogenous TME concentration.\n\nNow let me also check P0593 (allopurinol/inosine). This is in U3_2's supporting studies. It provides indirect evidence for inosine's role via xanthine oxidase inhibition. This is relevant but should be carefully framed as indirect.\n\nLet me now write the updated plans.\n\nFor U3_2:\n- substantive_point: Keep focused on inosine's mechanism (UBA6) and clinical association (CheckMate 025), with plasma proxy limitation noted\n- P01: UBA6 mechanism (P0582) - keep\n- P02: CheckMate 025 + plasma proxy limitation (P0582) - keep but tighten\n- P03: Distinguish mechanisms (P0124, P0251, P0584) - keep\n- P04: Reframe from \"TME gap + PK challenges\" to \"PK constraints on mechanism interpretation\" - focus on adenosine→inosine kinetics, ENT dependency, multi-source origin. Brief note that TME quantification is unresolved, pointing forward to U3_5.\n\nFor U3_5:\n- substantive_point: Keep as cross-metabolite TME concentration gap assessment\n- P01: Evaluate systemic exposure proxies (plasma/fecal) across metabolite classes (P0582, P0363) - broaden beyond inosine\n- P02: TME concentration gap as cross-metabolite problem (P0584, P0413, P0363) - use inosine as example but frame broadly, avoid re-explaining UBA6\n- P03: Future technical routes (P0582, P0363, P0413) - keep\n\nLet me now write the actual JSON. I need to be careful to:\n1. Keep all source_handles valid\n2. Preserve conditions and limitations\n3. Not add new sources\n4. Make the division of labor clear between U3_2 and U3_5\n5. Provide ordered paragraph_briefs with concrete points\n\nLet me draft the updated plans now.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the current U3_2 paragraph P04:\n\"综合 P0582 与 P0584 的讨论，指出腺苷快速降解（~10 秒）与肌苷较长半衰期（~15 小时）导致的测量窗口限制，以及缺乏原位微透析或空间代谢组学数据的现状，强调这是限制机制确证的关键缺口。\"\n\nAnd U3_5 paragraph P02:\n\"结合 P0584 与 P0413 的药代动力学与递送障碍分析，说明缺乏 TME 浓度阈值如何导致体外有效浓度无法在体内复现，以及为何单纯提高血浆浓度未必改善疗效。\"\n\nThe overlap is: both discuss PK/measurement challenges. The fix:\n- U3_2_P04 should focus on the PK features that are specific to understanding the inosine-UBA6 mechanism (why we can't validate the mechanism in human TME, the adenosine→inosine conversion issue, ENT transporter dependency). This is about mechanism validation constraints.\n- U3_5_P02 should focus on the broader translational implications: without TME concentrations, we can't do dose optimization, can't translate in vitro concentrations to in vivo, can't establish concentration-response relationships. This is about the translational gap across all metabolites.\n\nLet me finalize the plans.\n\nFor U3_2, I'll also incorporate P0588 (Phase 2 trial) more explicitly since it's in the supporting studies. The Phase 2 trial shows exogenous supplementation improves PFS, which is relevant to the mechanism discussion but also highlights that we're giving exogenous inosine without knowing endogenous TME levels.\n\nActually, looking at the current U3_2 cases, P0588 and P0593 are in supporting_studies but not in cases. Let me check if I should add them to cases or keep them in supporting_studies. The current structure has 4 cases and 6 supporting_studies. I'll keep the structure but may adjust.\n\nLet me write the final output now. I need to return a complete updated_plan for both U3_2 and U3_5.\n\nKey changes:\n1. U3_2_P04: Reframe from TME gap assessment to PK constraints on mechanism interpretation\n2. U3_5_P01: Broaden to cross-metabolite assessment\n3. U3_5_P02: Frame as cross-metabolite TME gap, use inosine as example without re-explaining mechanism\n4. Adjust synthesis and transition accordingly\n5. Ensure no source_handle changes, just reorganization of emphasis\n\nLet me write this out carefully.",
